%%{init: {"sequence": {"wrap": true, "width": 170, "noteMargin": 8}}}%%
%% Redis restart or wipe -> reconciler -> syncDropFromPostgres (section 4.7): drop lock, RECONCILING,
%% generation fence, snapshot, atomic fd_rebuild. Source of docs/diagrams/redis-rebuild.svg
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as worker reconciler
  participant R as Redis
  participant P as Postgres
  participant A as api (reserve in flight)
  participant S as settlement consumer

  Note over A,R: Before the restart, A got RESERVED with gen 7 from fd_reserve
  C->>R: every 2 s: INFO server run_id, GET fd:epoch, FUNCTION LIST flashdrop
  R-->>C: run_id changed (AOF tail may be lost) or fd:epoch missing (keyspace wiped)
  C->>R: FUNCTION LOAD REPLACE flashdrop, if missing
  loop every tracked drop, read from Postgres (not DRAFT, now < ends_at + 24 h), ENDED ones included
    C->>P: pg_advisory_lock(fd.sync:dropId) on a dedicated session
    Note over C,P: Admin arm / reconcile / pause / resume / end and the scheduler take the same lock, so the drop's Redis status can't change until unlock
    C->>R: fd_set_status RECONCILING (creates a fail-closed inv hash if it is missing)
    Note over R: Every Function on this drop now answers RETRY. Reserve → 503 Retry-After 1, settlement pauses its partition
    C->>P: UPDATE drop_inventory SET redis_gen = redis_gen + 1 → 8, COMMIT
    A->>P: reserve txn: INSERT order, quota, outbox, UPDATE drop_inventory WHERE redis_gen = 7
    P-->>A: 0 rows → STALE_GEN, ROLLBACK
    Note over A: 503, retry with the same key. The rebuild never counted this hold and discards its rsv entry
    C->>P: REPEATABLE READ snapshot: drop, inventory, quotas, every order of the drop
    S->>R: FCALL fd_release for an order settled in PG after the snapshot
    R-->>S: RETRY, partition paused and retried with backoff
    C->>R: FCALL fd_rebuild(snapshot, gen 8)
    Note over R,P: Validates the whole snapshot before the first write. STALE if gen ≤ the gen in Redis. Then DEL rsv uq exp, write inv, rsv, uq, exp and the status, and publish a snapshot frame (gen 8, seq 0). Clients drop anything older
    C->>P: pg_advisory_unlock
    S->>R: FCALL fd_release (retry)
    R-->>S: OK if the snapshot still had it HELD, NOOP if it was already terminal
    A->>R: client retry with the same key: fd_reserve
    R-->>A: RESERVED, gen 8, and the PG txn commits
  end
  C->>R: SET fd:epoch new uuid
  C->>P: store run_id and epoch in system_state
